-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat gpai from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-seat-gpai: the seat questions of Articles 1 to 4, 111 and 113 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744), asked by a provider of a general-purpose AI model, with or without systemic risk (Articles 3(3) and 3(63)).
--
-- LAYER 2 (the seat layer). Every question below calls a function of the keel (aia-scope, aia-definitions, aia-literacy, aia-timeline, aia-annex-x) and restates no rule.
-- The keel decides what the text means, the date it applies from and which text is in force; this file asks, in the words and with the facts of this seat, what a person in the seat can state.
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it. The role facts are asked once, in the question under Article 3 (or Article 2 for a product manufacturer and a person affected),
-- and no other question asks them again; where a keel function needs the role as a fact, this file passes TRUE.
--
-- THE DATE ASKED. Every question whose answer depends on a date asks `the date asked`. It selects the text in force (the Regulation as enacted until 26 July 2026, as amended from 27 July 2026,
-- the day the Omnibus enters into force) and whether the provision applies yet (Chapter I from 2 February 2025; the group General from 2 August 2026).
-- The other shared inputs (the placement date, the significant-change flag, the route by which the AI system is high-risk) carry the same name and @desc in every question that needs them.
--
-- RESULTS. A MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE DATE answer of NOTHING means "not covered": the provision does not speak to these facts, or has not begun to apply, or is not in the text in force on the date asked.
-- JUST FALSE is the text's own "no" (a flat negative such as "does not apply", or a condition it states). The answer of a keel function is passed through unchanged; nothing here turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- An exported obligation (a DEONTIC answer) is shown by a form as the placeholder "<obligation>"; its content is read with #TRACE in the case file.
--
-- STATUS. Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect (it says so itself, line 2 of the file).
-- The readings are the keel's (NOTES.md, fork register) and this layer's (NOTES.md, fork register P0): assumed, not ruled by a lawyer.
-- The Interact form and jl4-service were not run; l4 check, l4 run and l4 batch were.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`
-- Chapter I (Articles 1 to 4a) applies from 2 February 2025 (Art 113 third paragraph, point (a)).
-- Article 1 itself creates no rule (a purpose clause and a statement of contents): the one question a seat asks of it is whether the Chapter it opens applies.

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1660 | (a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025, with the exception of Article 5(1), first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb), and Article 5(1a) and (1b) which shall apply from 2 December 2026;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202 | Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025;
@ref Art 113 first paragraph and third paragraph point (a): Chapter I (src:1656) (src:1660) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202)
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).
@export Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 1, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Article 2(1): does the Regulation apply to me?`
-- Article 2(1) lists whom the Regulation applies to; a seat asks the limb that names its role.
-- A party outside every limb is "not covered" (NOTHING): the list does not close.

-- src:33 | (a) providers placing on the market or putting into service AI systems or placing on the market general-purpose AI models in the Union, irrespective of whether those providers are established or located within the Union or in a third country;
@ref Art 2(1)(a) (src:33)
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it, so the keel's role fact is passed as TRUE. Whether the definition of the role fits is asked once, in the question under Article 3.
-- The place of establishment is not asked: the limb reaches providers in the Union and in a third country alike.
@export Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `I place the general-purpose AI model on the market in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you place the general-purpose AI model on the market in the Union? It does not matter whether you are established in the Union or in a third country.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(1)(a), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to me` IS
    `Art 2(1)(a) the Regulation applies to the provider` `the date asked` TRUE FALSE `I place the general-purpose AI model on the market in the Union`


§ `Article 2(6): AI systems and models developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development`
-- Only if the AI system or model was developed and put into service for that purpose alone.

-- src:48 | 6. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems or AI models, including their output, specifically developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development.
@ref Art 2(6) (src:48)
-- The seat assumes the thing asked about is an AI model (the keel's first fact is passed as TRUE); whether software is an AI system is asked under Article 3(1).
@export Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI model was specifically developed and put into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the AI model specifically developed and put into service?
      `the AI model was so developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the AI model developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development? Answer no if it serves any other purpose too.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(6), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to the AI model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` IS
    `Art 2(6) the Regulation applies to the AI system or model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` `the date asked` TRUE `the AI model was specifically developed and put into service` `the AI model was so developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development`


§ `Article 2(8): research, testing and development before placing on the market`
-- Only if you carry out research, testing or development before the AI system or model is placed on the market or put into service.

-- src:52 | 8. This Regulation does not apply to any research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models prior to their being placed on the market or put into service. Such activities shall be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law. Testing in real world conditions shall not be covered by that exclusion.
@ref Art 2(8) first and third sentences (src:52)
@export Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `my activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your activity a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models?
      `it is carried out before the AI system or model is placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it carried out before the AI system or model is placed on the market or put into service?
      `it is testing in real world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it testing in real world conditions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the Regulation apply to my research, testing or development activity` IS
    `Art 2(8) the Regulation applies to the research, testing or development activity` `the date asked` `my activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models` `it is carried out before the AI system or model is placed on the market or put into service` `it is testing in real world conditions`

-- src:52 | 8. This Regulation does not apply to any research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models prior to their being placed on the market or put into service. Such activities shall be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law. Testing in real world conditions shall not be covered by that exclusion.
@ref Art 2(8) second sentence (src:52)
-- A "shall" with no time limit and no stated consequence: there is no breach path, so the answer says only that the duty exists.
@export Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `my activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your activity a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models?
      `it is carried out before the AI system or model is placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it carried out before the AI system or model is placed on the market or put into service?
      `it is testing in real world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it testing in real world conditions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, must my research, testing or development activity be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` IS
    `Art 2(8) the activity must be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law` `the date asked` `my activity is a research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models` `it is carried out before the AI system or model is placed on the market or put into service` `it is testing in real world conditions`


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`
-- The role question of the seat: the other questions of this file assume the answer is yes.

-- src:68 | (3) ‘provider’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body that develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model or that has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed and places it on the market or puts the AI system into service under its own name or trademark, whether for payment or free of charge;
@ref Art 3(3) (src:68)
-- The role question of this seat. Fork F-3-3 of the keel: whoever develops or has developed AND places it on the market (or puts it into service) under its own name or trademark.
@export Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me?
GIVEN `I develop the general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you develop the general-purpose AI model yourself?
      `I have the general-purpose AI model developed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the general-purpose AI model developed for you by someone else?
      `I place the general-purpose AI model on the market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you place the general-purpose AI model on the market?
      `I do so under my own name or trademark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do so under your own name or trademark?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does the definition of a provider fit me` IS
    `Art 3(3) the party is a provider` `I develop the general-purpose AI model` `I have the general-purpose AI model developed` `I place the general-purpose AI model on the market` `I do so under my own name or trademark`

-- src:73 | (8) ‘operator’ means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor;
@ref Art 3(8) (src:73)
-- No fact is asked: the seat fixes the role passed to the keel (a person who holds another role asks that seat's question).
@export Under Article 3(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I an operator?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(8), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I an operator` IS
    `Art 3(8) the role is an operator` Provider


§ `Article 3(9) to (11): placing on the market, making available on the market, putting into service`
-- These fix the dates the other questions ask for ("the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service").

-- src:74 | (9) ‘placing on the market’ means the first making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market;
@ref Art 3(9) (src:74)
@export Under Article 3(9), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my supply of the general-purpose AI model a placing on the market?
GIVEN `my supply is a making available of the general-purpose AI model on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your supply a making available of the general-purpose AI model on the Union market?
      `it is the first making available of the general-purpose AI model on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the first making available of that general-purpose AI model on the Union market?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(9), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my supply of the general-purpose AI model a placing on the market` IS
    `Art 3(9) the supply is a placing on the market` `my supply is a making available of the general-purpose AI model on the Union market` `it is the first making available of the general-purpose AI model on the Union market`


