§ `Article 3(63): is my model a general-purpose AI model?`
-- The model question of the model provider seat.

-- src:144 | (63) ‘general-purpose AI model’ means an AI model, including where such an AI model is trained with a large amount of data using self-supervision at scale, that displays significant generality and is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks regardless of the way the model is placed on the market and that can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications, except AI models that are used for research, development or prototyping activities before they are placed on the market;
@ref Art 3(63) (src:144)
@export Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model?
GIVEN `the model is an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model an AI model?
      `it displays significant generality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it display significant generality?
      `it is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks?
      `it can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications?
      `it is used for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(63), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, is my model a general-purpose AI model` IS
    `Art 3(63) the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is an AI model` `it displays significant generality` `it is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks` `it can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications` `it is used for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market`


§ `Article 111(3): general-purpose AI models already on the market`
-- Only if the model was placed on the market before 2 August 2025.

-- src:1625 | 3. Providers of general-purpose AI models that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2025 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2027.
@ref Art 111(3) (src:1625)
@export Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the general-purpose AI model first placed on the market in the Union?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, by what date must I take the necessary steps to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation` IS
    `Art 111(3) the date by which the provider of a general-purpose AI model already on the market must comply` `the date asked` `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market`

-- src:1625 | 3. Providers of general-purpose AI models that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2025 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2027.
@ref Art 111(3) (src:1625)
-- The deadline is a computed WITHIN (2 August 2027 minus the day the Regulation enters into force), so the clock of a trace starts at 1 August 2024 (day 0).
@export Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the general-purpose AI model first placed on the market in the Union?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 111 act`
DECIDE `Under Article 111(3), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, what must I do to comply with the obligations laid down in the Regulation on the date asked` IS
    `Art 111(3) the duty of the provider of a general-purpose AI model already on the market` `the date asked` `the date the general-purpose AI model was placed on the market`


§ `Article 111 and Article 113: does the group General apply on the date asked?`
-- The group General holds every provision that no point of Article 113 dates separately, among them Articles 111 to 113 themselves: it applies from 2 August 2026 (Art 113, second paragraph).
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1657 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2199 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
@ref Art 113 first and second paragraphs: the group General (Articles 111 to 113 and every provision no point of Article 113 dates) (src:1656-1657) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198-2199)
-- A legacy high-risk AI system saved by Article 111(2) is a separate question (Under Article 111(2), first sentence).
@export Under Article 111, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 111, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat gpai from part P2 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P2-seat-gpai.l4: the seat of a provider of a general-purpose AI model, over the layer-1 modules of part P2 (Article 4a, Articles 8 to 15, Annex IV).
-- It calls the layer-1 rules and never restates one. Every question has @export and @desc and takes plain inputs; the records a rule expects are built in a WHERE.
-- The shared inputs have the same names and @desc in every question: the date asked; the route by which the AI system is high-risk; the date it was placed on the market or put into service; whether its design was significantly changed since Chapter III applied.
-- A result of NOTHING is "not covered" (not yet applicable, saved by Article 111(2), or outside what the text says); JUST FALSE is the text's own "no".
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it (the role question below calls the keel's definition once).

§ `The role and the applicability of the provisions`

@export Under Article 4a, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a provider of a general-purpose AI model within the meaning of Article 3(3) and (63)?
GIVEN `the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you develop the general-purpose AI model?
      `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the general-purpose AI model developed for you?
      `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you place the model on the market?
      `the party does so under its own name or trademark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do so under your own name or trademark?
      `the model is an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an AI model?
      `it displays significant generality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it display significant generality?
      `it is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks?
      `it can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications?
      `it is used for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used only for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, am I a provider of a general-purpose AI model within the meaning of Article 3(3) and (63)` IS
    JUST (`Art 3(3) the party is a provider` `the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed` `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service` `the party does so under its own name or trademark` AND `Art 3(63) the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is an AI model` `it displays significant generality` `it is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks` `it can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications` `it is used for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market`)

@export Under Article 4a, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a, as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Under Article 4a: processing special categories of personal data for bias detection and correction`

@export Under Article 4a(2), as a provider of a general-purpose AI model, may I exceptionally process special categories of personal data to ensure bias detection and correction?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the category is referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade union membership, genetic or biometric data, health, sex life or sexual orientation)?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725?
      `such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations?
      `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place?
